A||||7||Seanh||Auto Dimming Rearview mirror||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||10-21-2000||12:48 PM||||I was wanting to do this on my Fiero. What cars do they come on? I would like one that auto dims, has a digital compass and temp, and maybe even a volt meter. I saw one that some one made them selves. They took a piece of two way mirror and put a green digital volt meter and temp guage behind it. You flip a switch to turn them on or off. I would do this, but I would also like one that has the auto dimming feature on it. Any Ideas?<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000001||BAM-BAM||10-21-2000||02:15 PM||||  GM has them on the Suburban, Yukon, Tahoe and Cadillacs have them. Cadillac also has the one with the GPS built in . The one you are talking about is about $340.00 over the counter, but they go on E-Bay for around $100.00 pretty routinely.<P> Later, BAM OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>P.S. Do a search for Earne Moon, he has one on his GT.<P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! YEAH BABY-YEAH<p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 10-21-2000).]||||reg||12
Z||000002||lawrence||10-21-2000||08:13 PM||||I picked up an automatic rear view mirror with map lights at the junk yard for $25.  They had a whole stack of them there.<P>One of the best mods I did to the car.<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://www.webelectricmagazine.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.webelectricmagazine.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||10-21-2000||08:31 PM||||My "new" 1998 Grand Prix has the optional auto dimming mirror, but no temp or compass built in. The temp is displayed on the climate control panel. The Bonnevilles aften have these mirrors too. A guy at work has one in his Eddie Bauer Bronco. I'm assuming all the late model GM luxury full size sedans have them now, like the Buick Park Avenue, etc.||||reg||1
Z||000004||My7Fieros||10-21-2000||09:45 PM||||Believe it or not, some late 80s GTA Trans Ams had them..they just dimmed or moved upwards when bright lights hit them.<BR>Man I love those cars!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Seanh||10-21-2000||10:53 PM||||BAM-BAM, do the ones your refering to on ebay have a compass or temp on them? I really want one with those on them.<P>Lawrence, Think you could get me one of them mirrors if I cant find one I like here?<P>If it comes down to it, I would like to get one like lawrence has, and modify it but putting guages behind it, like the one I mentioned above. Wait a sec. somthing just hit me, Dodge Darangos have the mirror with a compass and temp on them, I drove one I was installing a stereo system in a few weeks ago, I am not sure if they auto dim though, I only drove it in the day time.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bill Osmer||10-22-2000||08:13 PM||||Seanh -<P>I've already done this to my Fiero - as was stated earlier, it's one of the best (and easiest) upgrades I've done to my interior. It's easy - just drop down to your local auto recycler, and find a Jeep Grand Cherokee, or any of several 90's model GM vehicles. It's just a 3-wire connection (and actually only 2 are needed - the 3rd turns off the dimming feature whne in reverse). You'll want to run a a switched ignition wire up to the mirro over head area to allow for switching via the key, but othether than that it's EASY!!!<P>LMK if you need more info<P>------------------<BR>Bill Osmer<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumcardsig2.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Bill Osmer (edited 10-22-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000007||88formula||10-23-2000||05:14 PM||||The Toyota Tundra I just bought has an auto dinning mirror with a digital compass and temp gauge built into the mirror. You can buy them from a Toyota dealer for about $250.||||reg||1
